\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Benchmark construction pipelines. (a)~Landscape: seeds, expanded via pre-check, LLM generation, and Validator/Judge gate. (b)~Process model and enrichment: one accepted model yields Enriched-ORD fields, a SKILL.md, and design-time activity cases. (c)~Runtime cases: the single-LLM baseline-solver difficulty gate applies only to the retrieval-driven modes (Skill-Adjusted, Dynamic); Skill-Guided is scored by routing alone and Out-of-Scope uses a programmatic absence check, so both bypass the gate.}}{5}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipelines}{{1}{5}{Benchmark construction pipelines. (a)~Landscape: seeds, expanded via pre-check, LLM generation, and Validator/Judge gate. (b)~Process model and enrichment: one accepted model yields Enriched-ORD fields, a SKILL.md, and design-time activity cases. (c)~Runtime cases: the single-LLM baseline-solver difficulty gate applies only to the retrieval-driven modes (Skill-Adjusted, Dynamic); Skill-Guided is scored by routing alone and Out-of-Scope uses a programmatic absence check, so both bypass the gate}{figure.caption.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Process-driven semantic enrichment of ORD. A process model is mapped onto a Clean-ORD resource; the mapping deterministically derives four typed fields (\texttt  {capabilities}, \texttt  {useCases}, \texttt  {partOfGroups}, \texttt  {processNext}) written back into the resource, yielding its Enriched-ORD state. The resource identity is preserved.}}{6}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:enrichment}{{2}{6}{Process-driven semantic enrichment of ORD. A process model is mapped onto a Clean-ORD resource; the mapping deterministically derives four typed fields (\texttt {capabilities}, \texttt {useCases}, \texttt {partOfGroups}, \texttt {processNext}) written back into the resource, yielding its Enriched-ORD state. The resource identity is preserved}{figure.caption.5}{}}
